  "answer_text": "To determine the repeatability of the measurement, I focused on a dark fiber-like sample visible in the microscope image at (pixel_x: 600, pixel_y: 300). After performing autofocus to ensure the laser spot was sharp, I acquired five consecutive spectra using a laser power of 20% and an exposure time of 2.0 seconds.\n\nThe intensities at the characteristic peak position of 1001 cm⁻¹ were extracted from the resulting spectra: [329.0, 271.0, 276.0, 281.0, 277.0] ADU. The mean intensity was found to be 286.8 ADU with a sample standard deviation (ddof=1) of approximately 23.86 ADU. This results in a relative standard deviation (RSD) of 8.32%.\n\n```json\n{\"rsd_pct\": 8.318658554224074}\n```",
